  "articleBody": "It's super frustrating when your soft-close drawers aren't doing their job, right? You expect that smooth, silent glide, and instead, you get a clunk or a drawer that just won't quite shut all the way. A lot of the time, this comes down to alignment issues. The slides might not be perfectly level or parallel, which can cause them to bind up. Another common culprit is a cabinet box that isn't square. If the cabinet itself is a bit wonky, it's really tough to get the slides to operate correctly. Sometimes, people install the slides too tightly, or they forget to fully seat the soft-close mechanism before tightening everything down. You'd be surprised how much of a difference a tiny obstruction or a screw head that isn't flush can make! If you're finding your drawers are still noisy or sticking after a bit of tweaking, it might be time to bring in someone who deals with these quirks regularly. HH Remodeling LLC has seen it all and can help you get those drawers closing just right.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}